{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779047843,"nonce":"FHW8bSD3MgYVgRQDQRaijpf6tJc=","title":"Feedbax provider manifest ingest compatibility","message":"## Parent\n- `2472c51` — Mandible plugin ecosystem and artifact store for research tool providers.\n- `de2f8ac` — Mandible graph workspace and provider/artifact substrate.\n- Feedbax roadmap: `fa3978f`, Phase 2.\n\n## Problem\nMandible's Phase 2 provider/artifact substrate can ingest a generic Mandible-shaped provider manifest with `entities`, `artifacts`, and `edges`, but Feedbax Phase 1 now emits native Feedbax provider and run manifests with a different contract shape.\n\nThe next Phase 2 slice should make Mandible ingest real Feedbax Phase 1 outputs directly enough to inspect them in the provider/provenance graph. Without this, the generic provider substrate exists but the Feedbax/Mandible vertical path still requires hand translation.\n\n## Scope\nImplement native Feedbax manifest normalization inside the generic provider/artifact ingest boundary, without hardcoding Feedbax UI behavior into the graph renderer.\n\nRequired support:\n- Accept Feedbax provider capability manifests where `provider` is a string such as `feedbax`, with capabilities, schemas, artifact roles, and entry points.\n- Accept Feedbax run/spec/report manifests with fields such as `kind`, `schema_version`, `id`, `status`, `created_at`, `provider_version`, `feedbax_version`, `provenance`, `summary_metrics`, `artifacts`, and spec/parent references.\n- Normalize Feedbax artifact references using `artifact_id`, `sha256`, `logical_name`, `role`, `media_type`, `size_bytes`, `storage_backend`, `uri`, and metadata into Mandible artifact records and graph artifact nodes.\n- Create graph entities for native manifest subjects: graph specs, training run sets, training/evaluation runs, analyses, and reports.\n- Create provenance edges from provider manifest artifact -\u003e subject entity, subject -\u003e artifacts, subject -\u003e parent/spec refs, and provider -\u003e manifest.\n- Preserve opaque provider detail JSON for later rich provider detail rendering.\n- Keep the API provider-generic: Feedbax should be the first fixture, not a Feedbax-only renderer path.\n\n## Verification\n- Add focused backend tests using representative Feedbax provider and training-run manifest JSON fixtures.\n- Verify provider-lineage graph contains provider, provider_manifest, run/spec/report-style subject nodes, artifact nodes, and provenance edges.\n- Verify native Feedbax artifact refs produce stable Mandible artifact IDs and do not require blob content to be uploaded again when sha256/uri are already provided.\n- Run the relevant provider/artifact tests and full Mandible build/test if feasible.\n\n## Done means\nGiven a small Feedbax provider manifest and training-run manifest emitted by the Phase 1 Feedbax contract, Mandible can ingest them through `/api/provider-manifests/ingest`, persist provider/artifact/manifest records, and expose provider-lineage/provenance graph nodes and edges without a hand-written Feedbax translation step outside Mandible.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}